hadiths[60]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah has pardoned my Ummah for what arises in their hearts, as long as they do not act upon it or speak about it."
"21","Zararah bin Abi Aufa narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) the same narration, and he did not narrate it as marfu'."
"22","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah has pardoned my Ummah for thoughts that arise in their hearts, as long as they do not act upon them or speak about them."
"23","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not tell you of something which, if you do it, you will love one another?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah! What is that? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spread salam (greetings of peace) among yourselves."
"24","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""He who has no trustworthiness has no faith."
"25","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""A fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, a thief does not steal while he is a believer, a drunkard does not drink wine while he is a believer, a treacherous person does not commit treachery while he is a believer, and no person commits robbery and plunder while he is a believer, such that the people's eyes are raised towards him and he is looting."" Ibn Tawus says: And my father said: When he does these (acts), faith departs from him. He said: Faith is like a shadow or something similar to it."
"26","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The eyes commit adultery (by looking), the legs and feet commit adultery, and the private part either confirms or denies it."
"27","Hammad bin Salamah narrated this hadith with the same chain, and he mentioned ""hands"" instead of ""feet."
"28","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning."" Ukasha bin Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with him) requested: Pray to Allah that He makes me among them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Make him among them."" Then another person requested: Pray to Allah that He makes me among them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ukasha has preceded you in this."
"29","A narration similar to the previous hadith is reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) through another chain of transmission."
"30","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Musa (peace be upon him) met Adam (peace be upon him) and said: Are you Adam, whom Allah created with His own hand, made His angels prostrate to you, settled you in His Paradise, and you caused your offspring to be expelled from Paradise? He (Adam) said to him: O Musa! Are you the one whom Allah distinguished with His message and His speech? So, was I created before the decree or after? He (Musa) said: No, rather before the decree. Thus, Adam (peace be upon him) prevailed over Musa (peace be upon him)."
"31","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah and Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with them) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting among his noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them), when a stranger would come, he would not recognize the Prophet (peace be upon him) nor would he know where he was, until he would inquire. We said: O Messenger of Allah! If we prepare a seat for you so that you may sit on it, so that a stranger can recognize you. So we made a platform of clay for you, and we used to sit on both your sides. We were sitting when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came to his gathering, and suddenly a handsome man, wearing the best fragrance and extremely clean clothes, arrived. His clothes were such that it seemed no dirt had touched them. He greeted from the edge of the row of people, and said: ""Peace be upon you, O Muhammad (peace be upon him)."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied to his greeting. Then he said: ""May I come closer?"" He kept asking to come closer, and Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Let him come closer,"" until he placed his hand on the knees of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Muhammad (peace be upon him)! What is Islam?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""That you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish prayer, pay zakat, fast in Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House of Allah."" He said: ""If I do all this, have I accepted Islam?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Yes."" He said: ""You have spoken the truth."" The narrator said: We did not like his saying ""You have spoken the truth"" (because he was the questioner). He said: ""O Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Tell me about faith (iman)."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""To believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His prophets (peace be upon them all), and in every kind of destiny."" He said: ""O Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Tell me about excellence (ihsan)."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""That you worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then (know that) He sees you."" He said: ""You have spoken the truth."" He said: ""O Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Tell me about the Hour (Day of Judgment)."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) lowered his head and did not answer him. He asked again, but the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not answer him. He repeated the question, but the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not answer him. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) raised his blessed head, swore by Allah or said: ""By the One Who sent Muhammad (peace be upon him) with guidance and the true religion, the one being asked (about the Hour) knows no more than the questioner. But it has some signs by which it can be recognized. When you see the shepherds of livestock boasting about tall buildings, and when you see the barefoot and naked ones become the kings of the land, and when a woman gives birth to her mistress (master), there are five things of the unseen which only Allah knows."" Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) recited this verse: ""Indeed, the knowledge of the Hour is with Allah alone, He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs... the All-Knowing, the All-Aware."" Then a cloud of dust rose from the sky, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""By the One Who sent Muhammad (peace be upon him) with guidance and the true religion! I do not know more about it than any of you. That was Jibreel, who came to you in the form of Dihyah Kalbi to teach you your religion."
"32","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One day, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was prominently present among the people, when a man came walking. He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! What is faith? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “It is that you believe in Allah, His angels, His messengers, meeting Him, and being raised again after death.” He said: O Messenger of Allah! What is Islam? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “That you do not associate anything with Him, perform the obligatory prayers, pay the obligatory zakat, and fast in Ramadan.” He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! What is ihsan? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “That you worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, then indeed He sees you.” He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! When will the Hour come? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The one being asked knows no more about it than the one asking, and I will tell you about its signs: when a woman gives birth to her master, and you see barefoot, naked people becoming the leaders of the masses, and of five things only Allah knows: surely the knowledge of the Hour is with Allah, and He sends down the rain.” Then the man went away. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Bring him back.” They searched for him but did not find him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “That was Jibreel, who came to teach the people their religion.”"
"33","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) one day said to his noble companions: “Ask me.” So they were afraid to ask him anything. Then a man came and placed his hands on the Prophet’s knees and said: “O Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Tell me about faith.” The narrator then mentioned the hadith similar to the previous one, and added: “And that you believe in being raised after death, and that you believe in every kind of destiny.” And whatever he would ask you, he would say: “You have spoken the truth.” And the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “When you see the naked, barefoot, deaf, and dumb (like animals) people becoming the owners of the land (country), and you see the shepherds of livestock boasting with one another in construction.” In this hadith it is stated: “That you fear Allah as if you see Him.” And in the hadith it is stated: “This is Jibreel.” Abu Zur’ah narrated: He wished that they be taught to ask him questions."
"34","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The Hour will not be established until the sun rises from its place of setting. When this happens, every person on the face of the earth will believe. But that will be the time when the faith of any soul will not benefit it if it had not believed before or had not done any good in its state of faith."
"35","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (Regarding the explanation of this verse « مَن جَاءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهُ خَيْرٌ مِّنْهَا وَهُم مِّن فَزَعٍ يَوْمَئِذٍ آمِنُونَ » “Whoever does good, there is something better for him, and they will be safe from the terror of that Day.”) He said: “By this, «لا اله الا الله» is meant.” And « وَمَن جَاءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَكُبَّتْ وُجُوهُهُمْ فِي النَّارِ » “Whoever does evil, they will be thrown down on their faces into Hell. (That evil) is shirk (associating partners with Allah).”"
"36","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""There are three types of people with whom Allah will not speak, nor will He look at them (with mercy) on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: an old adulterer, a lying king, and an arrogant poor man."
"37","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to his uncle (Abu Talib): “Acknowledge «لا الهٰ الا الله» so that I may testify in your favor on the Day of Resurrection.” He replied: If it were not that the Quraysh would reproach me, I would acknowledge it before you. Then Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: « إِنَّكَ لَا تَهْدِي مَنْ أَحْبَبْتَ وَلَـكِنَّ اللَّـهَ يَهْدِي مَن يَشَاءُ وَهُوَ أَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِينَ » [28-القصص:56] “You cannot guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills, and He knows best those who are guided.”"
"38","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When three things appear, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or had not done any good in its state of faith: the Dajjal, the Beast (Dabbah), and the rising of the sun from the west."
"39","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: When this verse was revealed: « وَأَنْذِرْ عَشِيرَتَكَ الأَقْرَبِينَ » ""And warn your closest relatives,"" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gathered the general and specific people of Quraysh and said: ""O Banu Ka'b bin Lu'ayy! Save yourselves from the Fire of Hell. O Banu Murrah bin Ka'b! Save yourselves from the Fire of Hell. O Banu Abd Shams! Save yourselves from the Fire of Hell. O Banu Abd Manaf! Save yourselves from the Fire of Hell. Fatimah! Save yourself from the Fire of Hell. I will be of no avail to you before Allah, except that I will uphold the ties of kinship."
"40","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever intends to do a good deed but does not do it, one good deed is written for him; if he does it, then ten good deeds are written for him. And whoever intends to do an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is written against him; and if he does it, then only one evil deed is written."
"41","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to taste the sweetness of faith should love a person solely for the sake of Allah."
"42","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever wishes to taste the sweetness of faith, then when he loves someone, he should love him only for the sake of Allah's pleasure."
"43","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The adultery of the eyes is looking, the adultery of the tongue is speaking, and the adultery of the hand is touching, and the adultery of the stomach, the adultery of the feet is walking. The private part either confirms it or denies it."
"44","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a date orchard in Madinah when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Hurairah! The wealthy will be ruined, except for the one who spends like this, like this, and like this—before him, to his right, and to his left."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) walked for a while and said: ""Abu Hurairah! Shall I not tell you of one of the treasures of Paradise?"" He said: "" «لا حول ولا قوة ولا ملجا من الله الا اليه» "" Then he walked for a while and said: ""Abu Hurairah! Do you know what Allah’s right over the people is, and what the people’s right over Allah is? Allah’s right over the people is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, and the people’s right over Allah is that when they do that, He will not punish them."
"45","Kumail bin Ziyad, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, a narration similar to this."
"46","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""People will ask you about everything until they say: Allah created all these things, so who created Him?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you are asked (such a question), then say: Allah existed before everything, He created everything, and He will remain after everything."
"47","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Whoever presents himself before Allah with three things, Allah will admit him to Paradise: he worships Allah alone, does not associate partners with Him, and maintains an attitude of listening and obedience."
"48","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""What answer did your Lord give you regarding intercession?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""By Him in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), their being stopped at the gate of Paradise is more significant to me, and my intercession is for the one who bears witness with sincerity that there is no deity except Allah, at a time when his tongue affirms his heart and his heart affirms his tongue."
"49","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The truest statement in the poetry of the Arabs is the saying of Labid: Behold, everything except Allah is false (perishable)."
"50","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The truest statement that the Arabs have spoken is the statement of Labid (the poet): Listen! Everything except Allah is false (perishable)."" Umayyah bin Abi Salt was close to accepting Islam."
"51","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Three things are from the practices of the Age of Ignorance: wailing, a person disassociating himself from his father, and his boasting over people."
"52","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Three actions are from the signs of hypocrisy, even if the doer fasts, prays, and claims to be a Muslim: when he speaks, he lies; when he makes a promise, he breaks it; and when something is entrusted to him, he betrays the trust."
"53","With this same chain, it is narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established as long as there remains a single man who professes 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah), or who enjoins good and forbids evil."
"54","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever possesses three things will taste the sweetness of faith because of them: Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything else, he loves a person only for the sake of Allah, and after Allah has guided him to Islam, he dislikes returning to disbelief just as he would dislike being thrown into the fire."
"55","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports marfu‘an that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah has withheld repentance from every innovator.”"
"56","With the same chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! You will surely enter Paradise except for the one who refuses."
"57","Narrated with the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange at its end."
"58","It is narrated from Abu Ja'far that he was asked about the statement of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him: ""A fornicator cannot commit fornication while remaining a believer, and a thief cannot steal while remaining a believer."" So Abu Ja'far said: This is Islam, and he drew a large circle. This is faith, and he drew a small circle in the middle of the large circle, and said: Faith is confined within Islam. So when he commits fornication and theft, he comes out from faith to Islam, and only disbelief in the essence of Allah can expel him from Islam."
"59","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The month of Ramadan is an expiation for the sins committed until the next Ramadan, Friday is an expiation for the sins committed until the next Friday, and the obligatory prayer is an expiation for the sins committed until the next obligatory prayer."" Then after that he said: Except for three persons: the one who associates partners with Allah, «نكث صفقه» and the narrator of «تارك السنه» stated: So we realized that this is a new matter, we said: O Messenger of Allah! As for associating partners with Allah, we have understood that, what is meant by «نكث صفقة» and «ترك السنه» ? He (peace be upon him) said: ""By «نكث صفقه» it is meant that you pledge allegiance to a person, giving him your right hand, then you break that pledge and fight him with the sword, and as for «ترك السنه» , it is to separate from the congregation of Muslims."
"60","With this same chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Tell me, what do you think about the adulterer, the thief, and the one who drinks alcohol?"" They replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are evil and there is punishment for them."" Then he said: ""Shall I not tell you about the gravest of sins?"" They replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Associating partners with Allah, harming one's parents, speaking falsehood, killing a Muslim, and slandering a chaste woman."
"61","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When two people love each other for the sake of Allah in Islam, then the committing of a sin by either of them creates discord between them."
"62","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When Allah created the creation, He wrote a writing and placed it with Himself above the Throne. In it was written: My mercy prevails over My wrath."
"63","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There is no contagious disease, nor is there any reality in bad omens. I like to take good omens."
"64","It is narrated with the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: Which Islam is the best? He (peace be upon him) replied: ""The one from whose tongue and hand other Muslims are safe."
"65","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: Two men were abusing each other, and one of them taunted the other regarding his mother. The matter reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he called that man and said: ""Did you taunt him regarding his mother?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) repeated this statement several times. The man said: O Messenger of Allah! I seek forgiveness from Allah for what I have said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Raise your head! And look towards this group."" He looked at the people around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Prophet said: ""You are not superior to any of these red or black people; superiority is only for the one who is superior in religion."
"66","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever brings a good deed will have a reward better than it, and they (the righteous) will be safe from the terror of that Day."" He said: That (good deed) is «لا الهٰ الا الله» , and whoever brings an evil (sin), their faces will be thrown down into Hellfire. He said: ""That (sin) is shirk (associating partners with Allah)."
"67","Sa’sa’ah bin Sawhan said to Abu Zaid: I do not love your mother more than you, while you love my mother more than me. There are two qualities I advise you with, so remember them from me: Have sincere friendship with a believer, and behave well with a wicked person, because a wicked person will accept your words through good manners, and a believer has the right over you that you have sincere friendship with him."
"68","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that she complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about the occurrence of evil thoughts. She said: O Messenger of Allah! Such thoughts arise in our hearts that it is more beloved to any one of us to fall from the sky than to express such a thought. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is pure faith."
"69","Qatila bint Saifi al-Juhaniyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: A Jewish scholar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O community of Muhammad! You are the best of people, if only you did not commit shirk (associate partners with Allah)."" He (the Prophet) asked, ""What is that?"" He said, ""You say, 'By the Ka'bah!'"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) paused, then said, ""When you swear an oath, say: 'By the Lord of the Ka'bah!'"" He (the Jewish scholar) then said, ""You are good people, if only you do not associate partners with Allah."" He (the Prophet) asked, ""What is that?"" He said, ""You say: 'Whatever Allah wills and whatever you will.'"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) paused for a while, then said, ""Whoever among you says, 'Whatever Allah wills,' let him then say, 'then whatever you will.'"
"70","Qatila bint Saifi Juhaniya (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: A Jewish scholar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), then the narrator reported the hadith similar to the previous one, and added this: Upon both matters, he said: Subhan Allah! Subhan Allah! (an expression of amazement) What is that? And he said: ""Whoever says, 'Whatever Allah wills,' then he should say between the two: 'Then as you will.'"
"71","Abdullah bin Yasar Juhani narrated: A woman from our tribe told me that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, delivering a sermon. He, peace and blessings be upon him, was saying: ""None of you should say: 'If Allah and so-and-so (had not done)...' If he must say it, then he should say: 'If Allah (had not done), then so-and-so.'"
"72","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he heard a man saying: ""Evil is not according to decree (qadar)."" So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""Between us and the people of Qadar is the statement of Allah, the Exalted: 'The polytheists will say: If Allah had willed, we would not have committed shirk, nor would our forefathers.' He recited up to: 'If He had willed, He would have guided you all.' Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: 'Inability and wisdom are from decree (qadar).'"
"73","Ibn Tawus, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Those who speak about predestination speak without knowledge. Speaking about predestination—he said: Iblis met ‘Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, and said to him: Do you not know that only what is written in your destiny will happen? Go to the top of the mountain and throw yourself down from there, and then see whether you remain alive or not. So ‘Isa, peace be upon him, said: “Allah says: It is not appropriate for a servant to test Me; I do whatever I will.”"
"74","Az-Zuhri, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated: Iblis met ‘Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him, and he mentioned the same example. And he narrated that ‘Isa, peace be upon him, said to him: A servant cannot test his Lord, but Allah can test His servant. Then they debated and discussed with each other."
"75","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Mu’adh (may Allah be pleased with him) towards Yemen, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: “You are going to a people of the Book, so (first of all) invite them to testify that there is no deity except Allah. If they accept this invitation from you, then inform them that Allah has made charity obligatory upon them in their wealth; it will be taken from their wealthy and given back to their poor. If they accept this from you, then avoid taking the best of their wealth, and beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for there is no barrier between it and Allah.”"
"76","Muhammad ibn Ubaid al-Makki narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), it was said to him: A man has come to us, he speaks about predestination (qadar). So Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Show him to me, I will seize him by the head. By Allah! If his neck comes into my hand, I will break it, and if his nose comes into my mouth, I will bite it off, because I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""It is as if I am with the women of Banu Fahm, they are circling with Khazraj (as if their buttocks are colliding in a state of shirk). By Allah! Their evil opinion about them will not end until they exclude Allah from decreeing good, just as they have excluded Him from decreeing evil."
"77","Mujahid bin Jabr (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to this."
"78","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Five things have been given to me which were not given to any prophet before me, and I do not boast about it: I have been sent to the red and the black, whereas the prophets before me were sent specifically to their own people, but I have been sent generally to all people; I have been helped through awe, which precedes me by a month's journey; the entire earth has been made a place of prostration and a means of purification for me; spoils of war have been made lawful for me, which were not lawful for anyone before me; intercession has been given to me, and I have kept it in store for my Ummah, and it will be granted to every person who does not associate anything with Allah."
"79","Ubaidi bin Umair narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) a similar narration. The narrator stated, Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) used to say: By ""red and black"" is meant the jinn and mankind."
